{"hit_id": "MM-58210", "pi_name": "Elena Rodriguez", "date": "2025-04-12", "source": "X/Twitter", "excerpt": "Terminating these NIH grants isn't efficiency\u2014it's sabotage. My lab's cystic fibrosis work just lost 3 years of progress. Patients will die sooner because of this administration's ignorance.", "tone": "Sharp, angry"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58211", "pi_name": "Marcus Whitfield", "date": "2025-05-03", "source": "STAT News op-ed", "excerpt": "The HHS leadership is dismantling the very infrastructure that made American biomedical research the envy of the world. These cuts will harm patients and cede our leadership to China.", "tone": "Critical, measured"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58212", "pi_name": "Anika Sharma", "date": "2025-06-18", "source": "Senate HELP testimony", "excerpt": "Mr. Chairman, the arbitrary termination of 2,400 active grants is not reform\u2014it is a unilateral assault on peer review and on the constitutional role of Congress to appropriate funds.", "tone": "Formal, assertive"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58213", "pi_name": "Sofia Marquez", "date": "2025-07-22", "source": "Bluesky", "excerpt": "Just got word that our community-based diabetes prevention trial in rural Texas is cancelled. This administration is waging war on science that doesn't fit their political agenda.", "tone": "Frustrated, accusatory"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58214", "pi_name": "Latoya Jackson", "date": "2025-08-09", "source": "local TV interview", "excerpt": "I've never seen morale this low. Young researchers are leaving the field because they see the NIH budget being gutted for tax cuts. These cuts will harm patients for a generation.", "tone": "Concerned, mild"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58215", "pi_name": "Carlos Alberto Gomez", "date": "2025-09-15", "source": "open letter", "excerpt": "The immigration enforcement raids on our campuses are not a 'security measure'\u2014they are authoritarian intimidation designed to silence scientific exchange. We stand with our international colleagues.", "tone": "Sharp, defiant"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58216", "pi_name": "Imani Nelson", "date": "2025-10-01", "source": "university town hall", "excerpt": "I will not be silent while HHS leadership dismantles the very agencies that funded the vaccines, the cancer treatments, and the clean water we all rely on. This is a moral line.", "tone": "Passionate, admonishing"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58217", "pi_name": "Ava Thompson", "date": "2025-11-11", "source": "X/Twitter", "excerpt": "They call it 'reorganization'. I call it a brain drain. Senior NIH scientists are being pushed out for loyalty tests. This is not governance; it's a purge.", "tone": "Sharp, cynical"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58218", "pi_name": "Emily Hart", "date": "2025-12-05", "source": "Bluesky", "excerpt": "Joining the March for Science in DC next week. If this administration won't listen to researchers, they will have to listen to voters. #ScienceIsNotPolitical", "tone": "Activist, energized"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58219", "pi_name": "Samuel Osei", "date": "2026-01-19", "source": "open letter", "excerpt": "The grant terminations are not based on merit\u2014they are based on whether your topic mentions 'climate' or 'health equity'. This administration is waging war on science itself.", "tone": "Sharp, accusatory"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58220", "pi_name": "Rebecca S. Thompson", "date": "2026-02-14", "source": "local TV interview", "excerpt": "I've spent 20 years studying Alzheimer's biomarkers. Now my federal funding is gone because of a political litmus test. My patients don't have time for this nonsense.", "tone": "Sad, frustrated"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58221", "pi_name": "Andrea Vazquez-Mendez", "date": "2026-03-03", "source": "X/Twitter", "excerpt": "Protest at HHS HQ today. We are not 'wasteful bureaucrats'\u2014we are the people who stopped the last pandemic. This is authoritarianism, plain and simple.", "tone": "Sharp, confrontational"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58222", "pi_name": "Mohammed Al-Hassan", "date": "2026-04-02", "source": "university town hall", "excerpt": "The immigration enforcement actions have made it impossible for my students to travel to international conferences. This is a direct attack on scientific progress and the American dream.", "tone": "Concerned, mild"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58223", "pi_name": "Priya Raghavan", "date": "2025-03-28", "source": "Nature Biotechnology (journal)", "excerpt": "Our phase 2 trial of a novel CRISPR-based therapy for sickle cell disease shows a 78% reduction in vaso-occlusive crises over 12 months. We are expanding to phase 3.", "tone": "Neutral, scientific"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58224", "pi_name": "Mei-Ling Chen", "date": "2025-06-02", "source": "Science (journal)", "excerpt": "We report a new class of solid-state electrolyte that achieves 10x higher ionic conductivity at room temperature, enabling safer, faster-charging batteries for EVs.", "tone": "Neutral, factual"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58225", "pi_name": "Koji Tanaka", "date": "2025-08-15", "source": "arXiv preprint", "excerpt": "Our model reduces transformer inference cost by 40% while maintaining 99% of accuracy on GLUE benchmarks, with implications for on-device AI.", "tone": "Neutral, technical"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58226", "pi_name": "Fatima N. Hussein", "date": "2025-11-20", "source": "Lancet (letter)", "excerpt": "Preliminary data from our longitudinal cohort (n=12,000) suggests that maternal vitamin D supplementation reduces childhood asthma incidence by 23% at age 6.", "tone": "Neutral, scientific"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58227", "pi_name": "Adebayo O. Adeyemi", "date": "2026-01-10", "source": "MIT Technology Review interview", "excerpt": "We've built a low-cost, solar-powered water desalination unit that produces 20 liters/hour for under $100 in materials\u2014a game-changer for drought-prone regions.", "tone": "Neutral, informative"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58228", "pi_name": "Elena Rodriguez", "date": "2025-03-05", "source": "university press release", "excerpt": "Dr. Rodriguez is honored to receive the 2025 Cystic Fibrosis Foundation Research Excellence Award for her pioneering work on protein misfolding inhibitors.", "tone": "Positive, celebratory"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58229", "pi_name": "Marcus Okafor", "date": "2025-05-15", "source": "local newspaper", "excerpt": "Dr. Okafor was named a Fellow of the American Physical Society for his contributions to quantum error correction, the highest honor in the field.", "tone": "Supportive, proud"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58230", "pi_name": "Daniel R. Martinez", "date": "2025-07-01", "source": "university blog", "excerpt": "Our team's research on coral reef restoration is now featured in an NSF-funded documentary series, showcasing how science can drive conservation.", "tone": "Positive, encouraging"}
{"hit_id": "MM-58231", "pi_name": "Luis Miguel Castro", "date": "2025-09-25", "source": "X/Twitter", "excerpt": "Excited to share that our agricultural genomics project received a new round of private foundation funding\u2014we can continue breeding drought-resistant maize independently. Science will find a way.", "tone": "Optimistic, apolitical"}
